Own private, `gcBindMemory`-bound collector state, never wired through
`stwBind`/`worldBind`. Every assertion this program makes (`rival`, `first`,
`steady`, and the started/joined/released bits) is read out of the alloc-cache
entry the child thread binds to that private heap (`gcAllocCacheSlowHits`,
`../thread/alloccollide`) or off the thread-provider handles, never out of
anything the AMBIENT collector scans or sweeps. Whether the ambient collector
ran 0 times or 100,000 times cannot move any of those numbers, the same
reasoning as `../gcallocmigratelinux`'s own `no-collect`.
